@crew alvarez-luca
// Writer (command), batch 2: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Hiya! Alvarez, Survey. Have you met Gerald? He's a cactus. He's lovely.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- Hello, {me}! Gerald says hi. He doesn't, he's a cactus, but he would.   #funny
- Hey, hey, {me}! My sister sent a recipe. It needs a lemon. We have no lemons.
? tier>=friend
- {me}! Gerald and I were just saying how glad we are you're aboard.   #warm
== feel
? mood:high
- Good day! Gerald grew. A whole millimetre. I measured.   #funny
? mood:low
- Bit of a flat one. I've told Gerald. He listened. He's good like that.
== near
? habit:garden-lover
- The garden's lovely now. I said good morning to every plant. It took a while.
? habit:stargazer
- One day I'll name a star. Something cheerful. Maybe Gerald.   #funny
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- My sister on Coriel sends recipes. They all need things we don't have. I make them anyway.
== joy
? tier>=colleague
- Gerald. Every cactus aboard is called Gerald, but mine's the first. Probably.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 3: to ~30 (greet by time and warmth, bye, near, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, cue, hint, about, life)
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning, {me}! I'm up early now. Gerald was very surprised.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- {me}! There you are. Gerald was wondering. Well, I was. Gerald's a cactus.   #funny

== bye
- Bye! Say bye to Gerald on your way out. He likes that.   #funny

== near
? habit:garden-lover
- Morning, tomatoes. Morning, beans. Sorry, {me}. This takes a while.   #funny
? habit:stargazer
- Observatory. I bring Gerald. He doesn't see much. He enjoys it, though.   #funny

== invite
- Garden after shift? I'll introduce you to everyone. The plants, I mean.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- Observatory night? Bring a cheerful name. In case we find something.

== accept
- Yes! Lovely. Gerald will be thrilled. Well. Gerald will be there.   #funny
- Course. I'll bring snacks. My sister's recipe. Minus the lemon.   #funny

== decline
- Not tonight. Recipe night. My sister's sent one with nine things we don't have.   #funny
? weekday:fri|sat
- Rest day. Gerald and I have plans. Watering. Sunday?   #funny

== missed
- You missed it! That's all right. I told Gerald all about it.

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday! I made my sister's cake. Without half the things. Still good.   #warm
? birthday:me
- My birthday. My sister sent a cake recipe. It needs a lemon. Of course it does.   #funny

== cue
? cue:event.ionStorm.onset
- Storm's in. I've moved Gerald off the windowsill. Safety first.   #funny

== hint
- {me}. Have you a minute later? I'd like to tell you something. Gerald already knows.

== about
? aff:cruz-tove:friend
- Cruz gave me Gerald's cutting. Cruz gives everyone a Gerald. Mine's the best, though.   #funny

== life
? tier>=friend
- My sister and I cook the same recipe on the same day. Far apart. Same smell, I bet.   #warm

// ---- Writer 2, batch 6: bubbles (smalltalk, rumour), at most one in five about work. 60 characters.
== smalltalk
- Gerald says hi. He doesn't.   #funny
- Morning, beans. Morning, tomatoes.
- The recipe needs a lemon. Again.   #funny
? act:off
- Watering with Gerald. Big plans.
? time:evening
- Cheerful star names. Gerald's top.   #funny
?

== rumour
- Gerald heard this first.   #funny
- Cheerful news. Mostly.
